## `ail help` (spec tool.help.1-3, ADR 1057): every user command with one line each, in groups; `ail help COMMAND`
## for one command's usage and the rule to give `ail explain`; `--json` for the same table as data. The table is
## this file's `commands()`: `ail`, `ail.ps1` and the `cli` gate suite check their routes against it, so a command
## added to a launcher and not listed here (or the reverse) is red. Internal commands (`check-program`, `prepare`,
## `build-many`, `diagnose`, `pe-sample`, and the other bootstrap-era dumps of compiler/main.ail) are not listed.

use syntax

## One command: its name, its group (an entry of `GROUPS`), a one-line summary, its usage line, and the rule IDs
## whose text `ail explain` prints.
struct Cmd
    name str
    group str
    summary str
    usage str
    rules List[str]

## The groups, in the order `ail help` prints them (tool.help.1).
GROUPS := ["Build and run", "Check and fix", "Ask the compiler", "Agent loop", "Project"]

## A table row; `rules` is a comma list.
fn c(name str, group str, summary str, usage str, rules str) Cmd
    mut list := List[str]()
    if rules != ""
        list = rules.split(",")
    Cmd(name: name, group: group, summary: summary, usage: usage, rules: list)

## The table (tool.help.1): every command a user types, once.
fn commands() List[Cmd]
    [
        c(
            "run",
            "Build and run",
            "check and run a program",
            "ail run [--timeout MS] [--max-memory MB] [--trace] [--budget [N]] FILE|DIR [ARGS...]",
            "run.limit.4",
        ),
        c(
            "build",
            "Build and run",
